  "narrative": "The new results strongly support assay-stratum robustness for the three unvalidated large associations while arguing against strong histologic-subtype modification. In the Avana-library stratum, MSI-high remains associated with very much stronger WRN dependency: R18 is +0.813 in the hypothesis direction, with a 95% interval from +0.778 to +0.847. This is many standard deviations relative to the WRN score distribution and far above any 10% relative benchmark. SMARCA4 loss remains associated with very much stronger SMARCA2 dependency in Avana samples: R19 is +0.776, interval +0.753 to +0.799, also extremely large. The reversed KEAP1/NFE2L2 association is similarly large in the Avana stratum: R20 is +0.796, interval +0.774 to +0.818, indicating weaker NFE2L2 dependency in KEAP1-loss tumors. These Avana-specific acceptances are not independent validation because they use the same overall data structure, but they reduce the concern that the original effects were confined to a small library subgroup.\n\nThe adenocarcinoma interaction tests are all near null. R14 through R17 are small, around 0.01-0.03 in signed units, with intervals spanning zero and mostly well below the magnitude of the main effects. These do not support additional subtype-specific interaction effects in this dataset, so the interaction claims are rejected and closed. This should be interpreted as absence of evidence for a large interaction, not proof that interactions are impossible. The large accepted main effects appear broadly associated across the dominant histology stratum.\n\nThe negative-control test is reassuring: R21 for research_marker_e on WRN is null, with a signed estimate of -0.013 and interval -0.036 to +0.010. It does not mimic the MSI-high/WRN signal. This reduces, but does not eliminate, concern that the accepted large associations are merely generic markers of hidden cohort or technical structure.\n\nSeveral exploratory hypotheses remain unsupported. ARID1A loss is not associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency in the full population: R23 is small and opposite to the anticipated direction. This supports specificity of SMARCA4 loss rather than a generic BAF-complex marker effect, although BAF independence tests H36 and H37 are still pending. MYC amplification is not meaningfully associated with POLR2A dependency: R24 is tiny. BRCA2 loss is not associated with KIF18A dependency: R25 is small and opposite to the anticipated direction. These claims are rejected and closed.\n\nThe EGFR signal remains uncertain. In KRAS-wild-type tumors, R22 is directionally supportive of stronger EGFR dependency but small: +0.016 in the signed direction, interval -0.014 to +0.046. Relative to the mean EGFR dependency magnitude, the point estimate is roughly below the 10% threshold, while the interval still admits a modest clinically meaningful effect. Therefore H30 remains unresolved. I request independent validation for H17, the reversed KEAP1/NFE2L2 association, because it is very large, biologically counterintuitive relative to the original synthetic-lethal expectation, and now supported in the Avana stratum. If validation is concordant, H17 can be accepted with independent evidence; if discordant, the reversal will be revised or withdrawn.",
